Good points, usernames and uid's.
Also, the game binaries must be file-compatible.
Some of the compile time options affect it, so you should have the game
compiled with mostly same options on both systems.
It is easier to control when you compile the game youself (just keep the
same source tree and compile it with the same options), but if I
understood right, in this case the game came from a Ubuntu package.
It might be a good idea to copy the game directory and try if it works
with the other distribution as it is.

